  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New Features:\n- publish outbox messages to multiple streams\n  Add AddStreamPostman overloads for a fixed IEnumerable<StreamId> and per-message destination selectors, with optional OutboxSequenceToken. Both the processor and provider builder can now publish the same payload to multiple streams in one registration.\n  Empty destination collections complete successfully without publishing and allow acknowledgement. Destination sequences are enumerated directly without copying or filtering, so repeated stream IDs cause repeated publications. Fixed sequences are retained and selectors are evaluated per delivery attempt. Publication or enumeration failures leave the item pending; retries repeat publication using the same outbox token at every destination.\n  A selector returning an untyped default can now be ambiguous. Use default(StreamId) for single-stream selection or return [] for an intentional multi-stream no-op.",
